                                                "sense_id": "f90a91c4-938c-3867-adf6-570fa651c1ac",
                                                "text": "The war years have not greatly altered running conditions on the East Coast route north of Edinburgh. It was never a racing ground, and the heavier loads and the possibility of indifferent coal have been only partially balanced by the increases in running times of the principal trains."
